@startuml sell-persistence-adapter
!include sell-style.puml
title <size:12><color:#087F8C>06 / PERSISTENCE</color></size>\nMap the aggregate, preserve its identity

participant "JPA adapter\nJpaPortfolioRepository" as A
participant "PortfolioMapper" as M #E6F3F1
participant "Spring Data /\nHibernate" as R
database "MySQL" as DB #FFF5DF
activate A
A -> M : toJpaEntity(portfolio)
activate M
M -> M : Preserve IDs\nUnwrap value objects\nMap holdings and remaining lots
M --> A : PortfolioJpaEntity
deactivate M
A -> R : save(jpaEntity)
activate R
R --> A : managed JPA entity\nSQL may be deferred
deactivate R
deactivate A
... At flush / commit ...
R -> DB : SQL including orphan removal
DB --> R : database result
note over A, DB
  PortfolioPort is owned by application.
  The surrounding use-case transaction controls commit.
  Domain objects are separate from the managed JPA graph.
end note
@enduml
